## Agent Governance Suite

This project uses AGS contract v2. Preserve user-owned instructions outside
this block; only an integrity-verified AGS init migration may replace it.

- The host interprets natural language and submits one typed Operation through
  the CLI or `ags_decide`.
- Effectful Operations return a sealed `action_ref`; consume it only through
  `ags apply` or `ags_apply` in the same workspace/host/session binding.
- Existing `## 任务卡` input is validated before classification. Task-card
  execution authority comes from its mode/topology/delegation tuple.
- A task card overrides workflow-playbook defaults. In particular, authorized
  parallel worktrees and a no-commit rule must not be silently changed to a
  serial, commit-based workflow.
- Third-party MCP registration is advice-only. AGS does not proxy it.

Canonical references: `AGENT_SUITE_PROTOCOL.md`,
`protocol/agent-task-protocol.md`, `protocol/task-routing.md`,
`protocol/runtime-adapters.md`, and `protocol/mcp-server.md`.
